      "message": {
        "content": "Now I have a thorough understanding of the repository. Let me generate the README.\n\n<readme>\n# DocGen — AI-Powered Documentation Generation Service\n\n[![Go Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/Go-1.25-blue)](https://go.dev/)\n[![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-green)](LICENSE)\n[![Docker](https://img.shields.io/badge/Docker-ready-2496ED?logo=docker)](Dockerfile)\n[![Redis](https://img.shields.io/badge/Redis-powered-DC382D?logo=redis)]()\n[![Asynq](https://img.shields.io/badge/Asynq-task--queue-00ADD8)]()\n\n**DocGen** is a backend microservice built in Go that automates software documentation generation using Large Language Models (LLMs). It consumes tasks from a Redis-backed message queue via **Asynq**, orchestrates AI-driven documentation pipelines, and stores the resulting documents in a database. Designed as an asynchronous, scalable worker service within a broader microservices architecture, DocGen integrates with an AI service, a gateway, and a database service to produce high-quality documentation for software projects.\n\n---\n\n## Features\n\n- **🧠 AI-Driven Documentation Generation** — Leverages LLM-based AI agents to generate comprehensive documentation from project source code and context.\n- **⚡ Asynchronous Task Queue** — Uses Redis and Asynq to process documentation generation tasks asynchronously with configurable concurrency (up to 5 concurrent workers).\n- **🔌 Microservice Integration** — Connects to multiple backend services:\n  - **AI Service** — for LLM-powered content generation\n  - **Gateway Service** — for routing requests to local agent components\n  - **Database Service** — for persisting generated documents\n- **📁 Code Context Awareness** — Accepts source code files as input to generate contextually accurate documentation.\n- **🧩 Prompt-Driven Pipeline** — Uses customizable prompt templates loaded at runtime for flexible documentation generation.\n- **🛡️ Graceful Shutdown** — Handles OS signals (SIGINT/SIGTERM) for clean worker termination.\n- **🐳 Containerized Deployment** — Multi-stage Docker build with optimized caching, non-root user, and minimal runtime image.\n- **⚙️ Externalized Configuration** — YAML-based configuration with environment variable overrides for all service endpoints (AI, Redis, Database, Gateway).\n- **📝 Structured Logging** — Logs with timestamps, dates, and source file references for observability.\n\n---\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\n                     ┌──────────────┐\n                     │   Database   │\n                     │   Service    │\n                     └──────┬───────┘\n                            │\n┌──────────────┐     ┌──────┴───────┐     ┌──────────────┐\n│   Gateway    │◄────│   DocGen     │────►│   AI Service  │\n│   Service    │     │   Worker     │     │   (LLM)      │\n└──────────────┘     └──────┬───────┘     └──────────────┘\n                            │\n                     ┌──────┴───────┐\n                     │    Redis     │\n                     │  (Task Q)    │\n                     └──────────────┘\n```\n\nDocGen consumes tasks from a Redis message queue. When a `docgen:instruction` task arrives, it:\n\n1. Extracts the project context (title, name, prompt, code files, project type)\n2. Reads a markdown-based system prompt from `internal/prompts/`\n3. Sends the request to the AI Service with agentic mode enabled\n4. Stores the generated documentation in the database via the Database Service\n\n---\n\n## Installation\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- [Go](https://go.dev/) 1.25 or later\n- [Redis](https://redis.io/) (for task queue)\n- Docker (optional, for containerized deployment)\n\n### From Source\n\n```bash\n# Clone the repository\ngit clone https://github.com/dongtandung2001/Doc-Agent.git\ncd Doc-Agent/backend/services/docgen\n\n# Download dependencies\ngo mod download\n\n# Build the binary\ngo build -o bin/docgen ./cmd/docgen\n```\n\n### Docker\n\n```bash\ndocker build -t docgen-service -f Dockerfile ../../\n```\n\n---\n\n## Configuration\n\nDocGen is configured via a YAML file located at `configs/docgen.yaml`. All settings can be overridden with environment variables (e.g., `REDIS_HOST` overrides `redis.host`).\n\n```yaml\nai:\n  host: \"localhost\"\n  port: 50051\n\ngateway:\n  host: \"localhost\"\n  port: 8080\n\nredis:\n  host: \"localhost\"\n  port: 6379\n  db: 0\n\ndatabase:\n  host: \"localhost\"\n  port: 9002\n  user: \"user\"\n  password: \"password\"\n```\n\n### Configuration Reference\n\n| Parameter | Environment Variable | Default | Description |\n|-----------|-------------------|---------|-------------|\n| `ai.host` | `AI_HOST` | `localhost` | AI gRPC service host |\n| `ai.port` | `AI_PORT` | `50051` | AI gRPC service port |\n| `gateway.host` | `GATEWAY_HOST` | `localhost` | Gateway service host |\n| `gateway.port` | `GATEWAY_PORT` | `8080` | Gateway service port |\n| `redis.host` | `REDIS_HOST` | `localhost` | Redis host |\n| `redis.port` | `REDIS_PORT` | `6379` | Redis port |\n| `redis.db` | `REDIS_DB` | `0` | Redis database number |\n| `redis.password` | `REDIS_PASSWORD` | `\"\"` | Redis password |\n| `database.host` | `DATABASE_HOST` | `localhost` | Database service host |\n| `database.port` | `DATABASE_PORT` | `9002` | Database service port |\n| `database.user` | `DATABASE_USER` | `user` | Database user |\n| `database.password` | `DATABASE_PASSWORD` | `\"\"` | Database password |\n\n---\n\n## Usage\n\n### Running the Worker\n\n```bash\n# Start the DocGen worker\ngo run ./cmd/docgen\n```\n\nThe worker will:\n1. Connect to all required services (AI, Gateway, Redis, Database)\n2. Start an Asynq server listening for tasks on the `default` Redis queue\n3. Log incoming tasks and process them with up to 5 concurrent workers\n\n### Task Payload Format\n\nTasks are submitted via Redis (using the Asynq client) with the type `docgen:instruction` and the following JSON payload:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"API Documentation\",\n  \"name\": \"api-docs-v1\",\n  \"prompt\": \"Generate detailed API reference documentation\",\n  \"projectType\": \"go\",\n  \"code_files\": \"path/to/source.go\",\n  \"children\": [],\n  \"parent\": \"\"\n}\n```\n\n### Submitting a Task (from another service)\n\n```go\nimport (\n    \"github.com/hibiken/asynq\"\n    \"encoding/json\"\n    \"github.com/dongtandung2001/Doc-Agent/backend/shared/pkg/clients\"\n)\n\n// Create a task payload\npayload, _ := json.Marshal(map[string]interface{}{\n    \"title\":       \"User Guide\",\n    \"name\":        \"user-guide\",\n    \"prompt\":      \"Write a user guide for the authentication module\",\n    \"projectType\": \"python\",\n    \"code_files\":  \"auth/login.py,auth/register.py\",\n})\n\n// Enqueue the task\nclient := asynq.NewClient(redisOpt)\ntask := asynq.NewTask(\"docgen:instruction\", payload)\ninfo, err := client.Enqueue(task)\n```\n\n### Output\n\nGenerated documentation is automatically stored in the database via the Database Service. The worker logs the storage result:\n\n```\nProcessing docgen task: Title=API Documentation, Name=api-docs-v1\nGenerating documentation for project type: go\nDocumentation successfully stored for: API Documentation (id=api-docs-v1_20250401_120000)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\ncmd/docgen/\n  └── main.go              # Entry point: initializes clients, starts worker\nconfigs/\n  └── docgen.yaml          # Service configuration\ninternal/\n  ├── config/\n  │   └── config.go         # Configuration loader (Viper)\n  ├── pipeline/\n  │   └── generate_doc.go   # Documentation generation pipeline\n  ├── prompts/               # System prompt templates (markdown)\n  ├── service/\n  │   └── docgen.go          # Service layer: Asynq worker setup\n  └── tasks/\n      └── handler.go         # Task handler & data models\nDockerfile                   # Multi-stage Docker build\ngo.mod / go.sum              # Go module dependencies\n```\n\n---\n\n## Development\n\n### Building\n\n```bash\ngo build -ldflags=\"-w -s\" -trimpath -o bin/docgen ./cmd/docgen\n```\n\n### Running Tests\n\n```bash\ngo test ./...\n```\n\n### Docker Build\n\nThe multi-stage Dockerfile:\n1. **Builder stage** — Installs protoc plugins, generates protobuf code, compiles the binary with `-ldflags=\"-w -s\"` and `-trimpath` for optimized size\n2. **Runtime stage** — Uses a minimal `alpine:3.21` image with a non-root `appuser` for security\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies\n\n| Dependency | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| [Asynq](https://github.com/hibiken/asynq) | Distributed task queue on Redis |\n| [Viper](https://github.com/spf13/viper) | Configuration management with env overrides |\n| [connectrpc/connect](https://connectrpc.com/) | gRPC client communication |\n| [Redis/go-redis](https://github.com/redis/go-redis) | Redis client |\n| [Shared Module](../../shared) | Internal shared proto definitions, clients, and utilities |\n\n---\n\n## Contributing\n\nContributions are welcome and appreciated! Here's how you can help:\n\n1. **Fork** the repository\n2. **Create a feature branch** (`git checkout -b feature/amazing-feature`)\n3. **Commit your changes** (`git commit -m 'Add amazing feature'`)\n4. **Push to the branch** (`git push origin feature/amazing-feature`)\n5. **Open a Pull Request**\n\n### Guidelines\n\n- Write tests for new functionality\n- Follow Go standard formatting (`go fmt`)\n- Update documentation as needed\n- Ensure the Docker build passes\n\n---\n\n## License\n\nThis project is part of the Doc-Agent microservices platform. See the [LICENSE](../../LICENSE) file for details.\n\n---\n\n## Related Services\n\nDocGen is part of a larger microservice ecosystem:\n\n- **[Shared Module](../../shared)** — Shared protobuf definitions, gRPC clients, and utilities\n- **AI Service** — LLM-powered content generation service\n- **Gateway Service** — API gateway for routing and orchestration\n- **Database Service** — Persistent storage for generated documents\n\n---\n\n*Built with ❤️ using Go, Redis, and LLMs.*\n</readme>",
